# Title: Suspicious File Encoded To Base64 Via Certutil.EXE
# ID: ea0cdc3e-2239-4f26-a947-4e8f8224e464
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2023-05-15
# Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1027
# Description: Detects the execution of certutil with the "encode" flag to encode a file to base64 where the extensions of the file is suspicious
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((cmdline:*-encode* OR cmdline:*/encode*)) AND ((cmdline:*.acl* OR cmdline:*.bat* OR cmdline:*.doc* OR cmdline:*.gif* OR cmdline:*.jpeg* OR cmdline:*.jpg* OR cmdline:*.mp3* OR cmdline:*.pdf* OR cmdline:*.png* OR cmdline:*.ppt* OR cmdline:*.tmp* OR cmdline:*.xls* OR cmdline:*.xml*)) AND ((process_name:*\\certutil.exe) OR (OriginalFileName:"CertUtil.exe")))
